      "body": "## Overview\n\nAdds conversion support for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (`DeepseekV41ForCausalLM`) by subclassing the existing V4 model. Most of the V4 path carries over unchanged.\n\nDifferences that needed handling:\n\n- Text parameters are nested under `text_config`, so they are promoted in `index_tensors`. Overriding `load_hparams` does not work, because `ModelBase.__init__` calls it explicitly rather than through the instance.\n- `num_hash_layers` is absent in V4.1 while the V4 path reads it unconditionally.\n- The FP8 scale block size is `[32, 32]` rather than `[128, 128]`. V4 hardcodes 128, and reusing that value rescales every dequantized weight without raising, so the block size is now read from `quantization_config`.\n- Indexer `k_norm` and `wk` map onto the existing `INDEXER_K_NORM` and `INDEXER_ATTN_K`. `attn.compressor.ape` and `attn.indexer.compressor.*` are absent in V4.1 and go unused.\n- Four new tensors for the engram conditional memory.\n\nThe two engram tables need a separate write path. Each is `384,006,168 x 256`, and the inherited FP8 dequant computes `weight.float() * scale` over the whole tensor, which is about 393 GB as float32 for one table. They are read in row blocks from the safetensors shard, quantized per block, and accumulated into a disk backed memmap. Their scale layout also differs: `[rows, 8]`, one scale per 32 columns of a single row, rather than the `[rows/32, cols/32]` tiling the linear weights use.\n\nDraft, because this is the conversion half only. A converted file does not load yet: the `deepseek4` runtime requires `output_hc_fn`, `output_hc_base` and `output_hc_scale`, which V4.1 does not ship. Posting it now so the tensor naming can be looked at before files are produced against it.\n\n## Additional information\n\nConverted `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash` end to end on one machine with 121 GiB of RAM: 1046 tensors, 507.9 GB at `--outtype q8_0` with MXFP4 experts, peak host memory under 8 GB above baseline. Output checked with `GGUFReader`, all 8 engram tensors present. Quantized further to Q2_K to confirm the file is well formed downstream. `Q2_K_S` and `IQ2_M` both report that they need an imatrix, which is not obtainable until the model runs.\n\n`model_arch` currently points at `MODEL_ARCH.DEEPSEEK4`. Whoever adds the V4.1 runtime should decide whether it warrants its own arch, and this label should follow that rather than lead it.\n\n## Requirements\n\n<!-- IMPORTANT: Please do NOT delete this section, otherwise your PR may be rejected -->\n\n- I have read and agree with the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- AI usage disclosure: YES. An AI coding assistant was used to write the converter subclass in `conversion/deepseek.py`, the four tensor entries in `gguf-py/gguf/constants.py`, and the registry line in `conversion/__init__.py`, and to draft this description. The design decisions, the debugging that produced them, and the end to end conversion runs were directed and verified by me, and I am responsible for every line submitted.\n",
