      "body": "### Name and Version\n\nI've been trying to reproduce the CLI server arguments using a `model.ini` file without success. Many weird things that doesn't work, and the file format is basically undocumented. \n\nHere's the working CLI:\n\n```bash\n# llama-server.exe --version\nversion: 9267 (2754ce1b3)\nbuilt with Clang 19.1.5 for Windows x86_64\n\n# llama-server.exe \n       -v -lv 3 \n       -m \"D:\\ai\\models\\Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP-UD-Q3_K_XL.gguf\" \n       --n-cpu-moe 17 -fa on -np 1 --no-mmap --mlock \n       --cache-type-k q8_0 --cache-type-v q8_0 \n       -c 65536 \n       --port 8081 \n       --fit off --no-warmup \n       -b 4096 -ub 1024 \n       --rope-scaling none \n       -ot \"exps=CPU\" \n       --spec-type draft-mtp --spec-draft-n-max 2 \n       --tools read_file,get_datetime\n```\n\n\nHere's the not so working `models.ini`:\n\n```ini\nversion = 1\n\n[*] \n# empty\n\n[Q36-35B-A3B-MTP-T]\nm = D:\\ai\\models\\Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP-UD-Q3_K_XL.gguf\nalias = Q36-35B-A3B-MTP-T\n\ndevice = CUDA0\nn-cpu-moe = 17 \nthreads = 8\n\nfa = on\nfit = off\nno-warmup = on\nno-mmap = on\nmlock = 1 \n\nparallel = 1\nrope-scaling = none \n\nctx-size = 65536\nctk = q8_0\nctv = q8_0\n\nbatch-size = 4096\nubatch-size = 1024\n\nspec-type = draft-mtp\nspec-draft-n-max = 2\n\n#temp = 0.6\n#min-p = 0.00\n#top-p = 0.95\n#top-k = 20\n\n#presence-penalty = 0.0\n#repeat-penalty = 1.0\n\n;tools = all\ntools = read_file,get_datetime\n\n#---------------------------\n# Something fucked up here\n# -v -lv 2\n#---------------------------\n#   0: generic output\n#   1: error\n#   2: warning\n#   3: info\n#   4: trace (more info)\n#   5: debug\n#---------------------------\n#verbose = on\n#verbosity = 2\n#log-verbosity = 2\n#---------------------------\n\n#ui-mcp-proxy = true\nport = 8081\n\n\n```\n\n\nI'm then trying to run it with:\n```bash\n# Trying:\nllama-server.exe --models-preset \"C:\\path\\to\\models.ini\"\n\n# But most of the settings are ignored, like:  port, ot, loglevel etc.\n\n# More success with:\nllama-server.exe --models-preset \"C:\\path\\to\\models.ini\" -v -lv 2 -ot \"exps=CPU\" --port 8081\n\n...\nHowever, there are errors and logs are still not respected.\n```\n\n\n- `loglevel` is not respected, neither from file, nor command line, when calling **ini** file. \n- `port` is not respected, and seemingly random ports are used , unless specified on command line. \n- `ot` (or `override-tensor`) is not recognized at all.\n- Output runs in debug or trace mode and it's impossible to see the error/warning flying by. \nRedirection to file is not possible because windows build doesn't respect [Windows output streams](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_redirection?view=powershell-7.6) and dumps everything to god-knows which one. \n\n\n\n\n### Operating systems\n\nWindows\n\n### Which llama.cpp modules do you know to be affected?\n\nllama-server\n\n### Command line\n\n```shell\nsee above\n```\n\n### Problem description & steps to reproduce\n\nsee above\n\n### First Bad Commit\n\nn/a\n\n### Relevant log output\n\nsee above",
