      "body": "### Name and Version\n\n./llama-cli --version                                                                                                    0.001s \nggml_vulkan: Found 1 Vulkan devices:\nggml_vulkan: 0 = AMD Radeon RX 7800 XT (RADV NAVI32) (radv) | uma: 0 | fp16: 1 | bf16: 0 | warp size: 64 | shared memory: 65536 | int dot: 1 | matrix cores: KHR_coopmat\nversion: 6637 (5f7e166cb)\nbuilt with cc (GCC) 15.2.1 20250813 for x86_64-pc-linux-gnu\n\n### Operating systems\n\nLinux\n\n### Problem description & steps to reproduce\n\nI've been testing some Mesa changes recently and I've found out that this commit https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/commit/a2d3cbac2a1b9bae50c80a5b512e8633a65f0d57 completely breaks the usage of ggml's vulkan backend when using coopmat.\nThis has been tested both on llama.cpp (the output becomes gibberish) as well as stable-diffusion.cpp (the output images are still noise or stop being deterministic with the same seed) and it only happens when coopmat is enabled.\nI'm reporting this issue here, instead of in mesa's repo, as I'm not sure whether this is caused by the subgroup logic in the vulkan backend or not (the commit affects radv subgroups). If that's not the case I'll close this issue and open one in the Mesa repository.",
